{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551779-elder-methuselah-canon-npcs-with-child-teen-girl-appearance","id":1551779,"title":"Elder/Methuselah canon npcs with child/teen girl appearance?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-06-19T23:59:47-07:00","id":1551779,"title":"Elder/Methuselah canon npcs with child/teen girl appearance?","content":"For my game inspiration I want to find npcs like this. As far as I can recall:<br /> <br /> Vasilisa the Nictuku (child, maybe female, male more likely)<br /> <br /> Apacia (late teens)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-20T00:30:01-07:00","id":1551780,"title":"","content":"Ur-Shulgi has a childlike appearance, well, to the degree that he looks human and not like a burned corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-20T03:05:35-07:00","id":1551782,"title":"","content":"<b>Neferu</b> is a 5th generation Folower of Set, leader of the Fire Court in Luxor, 14<br /> <b>Tiamat </b>(Lantla) is a 4th generation Ventrue, Child of Arakur of Ur whom she &quot;ate&quot;, who looks like a 17 years old girl<br /> <b>Mary</b> the Black (Ma-ri-ah), after a few diablerie a 4th generation Baali (or Demon, she became a Decani) in Constantinople by Night was depicted as a 15 years old girl<br /> <b>Petaniqua</b> is... a good question; by her own account she was born as Polyxena, the princess of Epirus ; Polyxena was described by the chronicler Malalas in his account of the Chronography as &quot;tall, pure, very white, large-eyed, black-haired, with her hair worn long behind, a good nose and cheeks, blooming-lipped, small-footed, virgin, charming, very beautiful, 18 years old when they killed her&quot; so... maybe 18?<br /> <b>Alexander</b>, a 4th generation Ventrue was (destroyed by the Gangrel Qarakh) a 16 years-old, as beautiful as a classic Greek god, with golden, curly hair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-20-2025, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-20T19:44:33-07:00","id":1551796,"title":"","content":"Add one, Drenis of Inconnu, late teen (transgender though)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-21T03:56:12-07:00","id":1551802,"title":"","content":"Are you only looking for female child/tenn NPC or also for male?<br /> <br /> When it come to famales:<br /> <b>Genia</b>, 6th gen Samedi, with an apparent age of 9, one of the Anathema of the Red List","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-21T11:06:39-07:00","id":1551804,"title":"","content":"Forum flag ate it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-22-2025, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-21T11:09:15-07:00","id":1551805,"title":"","content":"aaand the Forum ate it while I edited, I wil ldelete the og<br /> So...<br /> <br /> In 1st edition there was a passing mention of several Malkavians embraced as a child<br /> A little girl who sits on a swing and talks to the dead was one of them and a boy who hasn't spoken in a century is another - neither of them were named nor gaven a stat, were just a passing mention on the sidebar (or plot hook? It was long ago...)<br /> <br /> To be honest, missed the part about the gender, thats why I wrote Alexander<br /> If guys are fair play there is a ... maybe?<br /> <b>Matteo</b><br /> He is the 8th generation Child of Lucita de Arag\u00f3n<br /> Now he is a wild card, because he was Alfonzo of Venice (8th Generation Lasombra, Children of Narses) 's ghoul. He had been with Alfonzo since he was a boy and he turned him into a ghoul because he was proud of the boy's performance. This is more of implied but not man, not young man, but in both cases, he was refered as &quot;boy&quot;. It could mean he was very young. pre-teen and ghouls not really age<br /> <br /> <b>Zo\u00eb,</b> Acolyte of Anatole the Prophet. 10th Generation Ravonos from the Dark Ages Novels and the Low Clan Player's guide was described as &quot;Mid-teens&quot;<br /> <b>Enam bint Ayub al-Dimshaq, </b>a 10th Generation Banu Haqim from Veil of Night had the apparent age of &quot;late teens&quot;<br /> Veil of Night also mentions <b>Bistakh, Sword of Haqim</b>, a 9th Generation Banu Haqim with the apparent age of &quot;late teens&quot;<br /> From the same supplement <b>Sakan, Orphan of San'a'</b> , an 8th Generation Ray'een al-Fen (Toreador) had the apparant age of &quot;Mid-teens&quot; <br /> Again, fr\u200b\u200bom Veil of Night <b>Nadim ibn Nuri </b>a 9th Generation Venture age of &quot;late teens&quot;<br /> <br /> I know we are scrapping the bottom of the barrel with these, but they are mid or late teen looking vampires from the Dark Ages, and most of them sporting (if they survived) a hefty ~1000 year old age now, but at least older than the USA<br /> <br /> As a bonus there is <b>Ramona</b> ithe signature character for the Gangrel clan in Vampire: The Masquerade, who was born in 1980 and been embraced either '97 or '98 making her a 17-18 year looking Gangrel girl. Not a children, but teen , true and not an elder but she seen things and have a level of respect\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-21T22:03:53-07:00","id":1551810,"title":"","content":"I believe I recall Enkidu's &quot;Sabrina&quot; form being that of a 16-year-old girl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-21T23:37:47-07:00","id":1551811,"title":"","content":"Found a few more<br /> <br /> <b>Anna Sgorina, Byzantine Envoy</b>, 8th Generation Gangrel, Children of Baron Thomas Feroux had the apparent age of &quot;late teens&quot; in Bitter Crusade<br /> Interestingly, Bitter Crusades describes <b>Lucita</b>'s apparent age &quot;late teens&quot; as well (later she was ore of a 20+)<br /> <b>Erzebet Toth</b>, the Lesser Child, 8th Generation Tzimisce had the apparent age of &quot;late teens&quot; also in that Supplement<br /> <br /> In Jerusalem by Night there is <b>Hannah</b>, an 8th Generation Nosferatu with the apparent age of &quot;mid-teens&quot;<br /> Also, <b>Shahara al-Rashwa</b>, Courtesan, 10th Generation Follower of Set with the apparent age of &quot;late-teens&quot;<br /> And frotm he same supplement your &quot;jacpot&quot;! <b>Yasmina</b>, a 7th generation Ravnos girl who was &quot;not yet 10&quot; when was Embraced!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-23T10:29:34-07:00","id":1551826,"title":"","content":"Much to my alarm, this is in fact a frequently recurring motif in VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE (The next high profile elder who doesn\u2019t look like actual jailbait might even be the first).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-23T12:54:20-07:00","id":1551828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551779-elder-methuselah-canon-npcs-with-child-teen-girl-appearance?p=1551826#post1551826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much to my alarm, this is in fact a frequently recurring motif in VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE (The next high profile elder who doesn\u2019t look like actual jailbait might even be the first).</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, most humans everywhere in history have had a lower age limit for what counted as an adult fit for marriage or other responsibilities. It is historically sensible that many ancient vampires would be very young by our standards.<br /> <br /> Also, one of the key lures of vampirism is the ability to preserve the appearance of youth indefinitely. Wisdom, knowledge, skill, etc. can be learned afterwards. A youthful appearance, the best one will enjoy in life (not counting that sweet spot when one still has some youth left but has lived long enough to know how to dress, wash, wear make up, etc. to also present oneself better), cannot be recovered later except by trading dangerous favours with the Tzimisce. It's perfectly sensible for me that most vampires for most of history would embrace or ghoulify humans in their teens whenever possible, and I'd have vampires in US domains have a recurrent problem and discussions over contemporary American sensibilities towards age, at least when it comes to teenagers.<br /> <br /> As for pre-teens and younger children, their embrace would have been an oddity in most times and places. There are multiple obvious drawbacks and not many advantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-23T13:11:01-07:00","id":1551829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551779-elder-methuselah-canon-npcs-with-child-teen-girl-appearance?p=1551782#post1551782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Petaniqua</b> is... a good question; by her own account she was born as Polyxena, the princess of Epirus ; Polyxena was described by the chronicler Malalas in his account of the Chronography as &quot;tall, pure, very white, large-eyed, black-haired, with her hair worn long behind, a good nose and cheeks, blooming-lipped, small-footed, virgin, charming, very beautiful, 18 years old when they killed her&quot; so... maybe 18?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the character was retconned after her profile in Kindred's Most Wanted (I know she was updated in Dread Names, Red List, but I haven't read that), Petaniqua can't be that Polyxena. The Polyxena from Malalas's Chronography was the legendary daughter of the King of Troy (not a princess of Epirus) during the Trojan War. Petaniqua is supposedly Olympias, the mother of Alexander the Great, who was a princess of Epirus and named Polyxena at birth (Olympias can be confusing because she had four different names at different parts of her life: Polyxena, Myrtale, Olympias, and Stratonike.) In KMW her apparent age was described as &quot;30&quot;.<br /> <br /> Since the historical Olympias lived until she was 59, there's some discrepancy then with the character as described and the historical figure. However, Petaniqua's biography in KMW takes that into account. First, it says Olympias became a ghoul and second, it says Olympias was embraced after the assassination of her husband Philip II. While Olympias would have been closer to 40 at that time, not 30, her being made a full ghoul around 30 would have preserved her appearance to appear much younger.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the World of Darkness sourcebooks include various discrepancies like this to inform the well informed reader that the vampire was lying, and to take everything with a grain of salt. Petaniqua doesn't need to actually be Olympias, though she could believe that she is. I personally think it'd be hard for vampire Olympias to hide her true nature for twenty years, but at the same time the Masquerade wasn't back in the fourth century BC what it is now. It's your personal choice/taste here. Regardless, her appearance was clearly not of an eighteen year old in KMW.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-23T19:09:55-07:00","id":1551832,"title":"","content":"Age of Embrace is a rather complicated matter.<br /> <br /> On one hand, the apex of the human body is around 30 years, and that has always been well known, at least since Classical Antiquity. If a vampire wants the Childe to be in its prime, both physical and mental, they would look for someone at that age.<br /> <br /> But then we have what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16965\" data-vbnamecard=\"16965\">Hermeticus</a> said, preserving youth is a strong theme, both psychologically and as a genre thing. And for most of history, the apex of youthful appearance was around 15 years. Good appearance isn't necessarily youthful, but that's both common and in with the genre.<br /> <br /> In the end, yes, VtM usually follows the Anne Rice stylistic choice of young vampires, and that does mean <u><b>a lot</b></u> of children and teens, specially among Elders and Methuselah. Even most of those that are in their 20s arguably shouldn't, as they're more based on <i><b>modern</b></i> people in their 20s than people of their times.<br /> <br /> Either way, making a game with more vampires in their mid 20s to mid 30s is an option. It would mean a more mature vampire society, though, which may or may not affect some aspects of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-23T21:22:07-07:00","id":1551833,"title":"","content":"Don't be all that shocked if all the members of the third generation and most of the fourth generation are going to look shockingly young with many looking like young adults.<br /> <br /> So try to keep that in mind if you planning on making methsaulth's in your game as what we would view as shocking by 21st century standards would be considered normal for there world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 06-24-2025, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-23T22:01:46-07:00","id":1551836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551779-elder-methuselah-canon-npcs-with-child-teen-girl-appearance?p=1551832#post1551832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Age of Embrace is a rather complicated matter.<br /> <br /> On one hand, the apex of the human body is around 30 years, and that has always been well known, at least since Classical Antiquity. If a vampire wants the Childe to be in its prime, both physical and mental, they would look for someone at that age.<br /> <br /> But then we have what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"16965\" data-vbnamecard=\"16965\">Hermeticus</a> said, preserving youth is a strong theme, both psychologically and as a genre thing. And for most of history, the apex of youthful appearance was around 15 years. Good appearance isn't necessarily youthful, but that's both common and in with the genre.<br /> <br /> In the end, yes, VtM usually follows the Anne Rice stylistic choice of young vampires, and that does mean <u><b>a lot</b></u> of children and teens, specially among Elders and Methuselah. Even most of those that are in their 20s arguably shouldn't, as they're more based on <i><b>modern</b></i> people in their 20s than people of their times.<br /> <br /> Either way, making a game with more vampires in their mid 20s to mid 30s is an option. It would mean a more mature vampire society, though, which may or may not affect some aspects of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Islam, men and women in Paradise are going to be eternally &quot;thirty&quot;, in the sense of their being given the best age. Of course, the basis of Paradise in Islam is that the human being is rewarded with the beatific vision of God which outdoes all pleasures plus everything one would desire plus the heart being cleansed from hatred (which makes me think now that sadistic people who manage to enter Paradise, for example by recognising that their desire for the suffering of others is wrong and abstaining from it as much as possible, will be probably freed of that particular desire), therefore people who are not happy with their looks at 30 don't need to worry about being stuck with those looks forever. Some traditions even indicate people being able to choose their bodies or appearances in Paradise.<br /> <br /> This makes me think that one could have a particular group (probably Toreador) in the Ashirra who deliberately embrace people at the age of 30, as if vampires are somehow the People of the Garden (Paradise). They may also make ghouls of young boys based on the wild\u0101n of Paradise, young boys being the cupbearers and attendants of people there, and ghouls of beautiful women to correspond to the h\u016bris, the maidens of Paradise, who are however less beautiful than the believers themselves, who lived as humans in this world and then have been rewarded with Paradise. The only problem with this set up is that it makes it hard to promote ghouls through the Embrace since the age of ghouling and that of Embrace are symbolically meant to be different. <br /> <br /> A Tzimisce subfaction of this group may offer their gifts to allow &quot;believers&quot; to choose their body and appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-23T22:16:05-07:00","id":1551837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551779-elder-methuselah-canon-npcs-with-child-teen-girl-appearance?p=1551829#post1551829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless the character was retconned after her profile in Kindred's Most Wanted <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>True<br /> Cybele Malkavian/Baali status complicates Petaniqua's identiy a bit more; but she is probably a Baali apostate embraced by Malkav and re-embraced by Nergal<br /> Olympias (born in 375 BC) was 19 when she had Alexander in 356 BC, so very late teen at best even if she was turned right away, but could work if she was ghouled first by Cybele and she was the member of the Cult of Cybele, but I am grasping straws there and easier to admit I simply confused the two Polyxenas <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-25T13:45:21-07:00","id":1551864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551779-elder-methuselah-canon-npcs-with-child-teen-girl-appearance?p=1551828#post1551828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, most humans everywhere in history have had a lower age limit for what counted as an adult fit for marriage or other responsibilities. It is historically sensible that many ancient vampires would be very young by our standards.<br /> <br /> Also, one of the key lures of vampirism is the ability to preserve the appearance of youth indefinitely. Wisdom, knowledge, skill, etc. can be learned afterwards. A youthful appearance, the best one will enjoy in life (not counting that sweet spot when one still has some youth left but has lived long enough to know how to dress, wash, wear make up, etc. to also present oneself better), cannot be recovered later except by trading dangerous favours with the Tzimisce. It's perfectly sensible for me that most vampires for most of history would embrace or ghoulify humans in their teens whenever possible, and I'd have vampires in US domains have a recurrent problem and discussions over contemporary American sensibilities towards age, at least when it comes to teenagers.<br /> <br /> As for pre-teens and younger children, their embrace would have been an oddity in most times and places. There are multiple obvious drawbacks and not many advantages.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s an element of truth in that, but it\u2019s also true that those hungriest for the gift of immortality would have been those old enough to feel their encroaching mortality - and it bears considering that older candidates would have had more time to prove their quality AND accumulate the sort of assets &amp; connections which would help make them an especially attractive prospect.<br /> <br /> In the end, of course, the choice all depends on the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-27T12:11:54-07:00","id":1551884,"title":"","content":"Elaine Cassidy, 6th generation Tzimisce, childe of Velya<br /> Nicolai Antonescu, 6th generation Trememe, childe of Stromberg<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-28T05:40:16-07:00","id":1551897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551779-elder-methuselah-canon-npcs-with-child-teen-girl-appearance?p=1551884#post1551884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elaine Cassidy, 6th generation Tzimisce, childe of Velya<br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>The Children of Osiris dragged Kemintiri back after she became a Wight.<br /> Maybe one would be insane to do the same with Elaine...?<br /> I am not sure why anyone would do that with a 10 year old monster who spent her unlife as a Wight grafted to the back of her &quot;husband&quot; but she probably would fall again...<br /> Nonetheless it would be interesting<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-28T22:33:55-07:00","id":1551906,"title":"","content":"That could work, but I highly doubt her being accepted nor Velya making the trip to go to them.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-29T14:27:39-07:00","id":1551927,"title":"","content":"They sometimes take the initiative, that's how they did with Kemintiri to begin with. An &quot;ex-Tzimisce&quot; CoO could very well go after Velya, take Elaine from him against his will, and go through the process of bringing her back to Humanity.<br /> <br /> How likely it is? Very little, but it was unlikely in the first instance too, and yet it happened. The Children of Osiris are rarely used in the canon, but doing such a thing is well within their description and past deeds. And I disagree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> in one regard: if Kemintiri managed to not fall <i>completely</i> despite everything, there's no reason to think Elaine would fare worse (faring just as bad is already pretty bad).<br /> <br /> Not a plot for everyone's tastes, but that's <i>par of the course</i> for the CoO when they appear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T11:13:23-07:00","id":1552036,"title":"","content":"Lucita De Aragon was around 17 years old when Moncada embraced her in 1190. Then you Lucinda the Venture Justicar who has the appearance of a 16 year old girl.<br /> <br /> Michael of the Toreador looks younger then someone in his early twenties in some of the artwork I have seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T11:16:41-07:00","id":1552037,"title":"","content":"I'd say that Eliane Cassidy is to forgone to be helped to humanity by the Children of Osiris. Even before her embrace by Velya she was on her way to becoming a monster, they would be better off helping her sire if anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-03T20:15:52-07:00","id":1552049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551779-elder-methuselah-canon-npcs-with-child-teen-girl-appearance?p=1552037#post1552037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that Eliane Cassidy is to forgone to be helped to humanity by the Children of Osiris. Even before her embrace by Velya she was on her way to becoming a monster, they would be better off helping her sire if anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that Kemintiri also was, and it worked nonetheless. It's less that it makes a lot of sense, or that it is likely, and more that it is a perfectly viable plot given what already happened.<br /> <br /> Kemintiri was a Wight, she was directly tortured by Set, everything she was before was corrupted, she was completely cut off from everything and everyone that once gave her life any meaning. The point she reached was beyond recovering as far as anyone can tell, even today.<br /> <br /> And yet, it happened. She became a Low Humanity looney, true, who most of the time doesn't even remembers her current alias isn't a real person. But she isn't a Wight anymore.<br /> <br /> The reason for that to not happen again is zero, if the ST wants to run this plot. I'm not saying it should happen, or it's likely to happen, just that it can and would be entirely within precedent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-10T18:57:07-07:00","id":1558780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551779-elder-methuselah-canon-npcs-with-child-teen-girl-appearance?p=1551782#post1551782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Petaniqua</b> is... a good question; by her own account she was born as Polyxena, the princess of Epirus ; Polyxena was described by the chronicler Malalas in his account of the Chronography as &quot;tall, pure, very white, large-eyed, black-haired, with her hair worn long behind, a good nose and cheeks, blooming-lipped, small-footed, virgin, charming, very beautiful, 18 years old when they killed her&quot; so... maybe 18?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, wasn't Petaniqua supposed to be Olympias, aka, the mother of Alexander the Great, that would mean a very much adult woman in the 50s to 60s (though younger looking due to ghouldom and the embrace at somewhat uncertain points in time)?<br /> <br /> Ok, reliable narrator she is not, but her overall portrayal and images seem to point out to a very much mature woman.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}